Designing the 1B dense-equivalent MoE from the skill formulas (I couldn't execute `tools/moe_calculator.py` — no shell/file tools in this environment — so all counts are hand-computed with the exact formulas below).

**Design choice:** `hidden_size=2048`, `num_layers=16`, vocab 32000, expert FFN 4096. With 16 experts / top-2: activated = 1.14B (~1B dense-equivalent), total = 6.78B (9.2× the 0.74B dense baseline). Capacity factor 1.25 to absorb routing imbalance; aux loss 0.01; EP=8 on 8 GPUs (16/8 = 2 experts/rank = top-2, so per-rank params == activated params).

- Activated params = 16·(4·2048² + 2·2048 + 2·3·2048·4096) + 32000·2048 = 1,139,343,360
- FLOPs/token = 6·1.139e9 + 4·16·2048·2048 = 7.10 GFLOP

